      "text": [
        " مَنْ قَرَأَ إِنَّا أَنْزَلْنَاهُ ثِنْتَيْنِ وَ ثَلَاثِينَ مَرَّةً فِي إِنَاءٍ جَدِيدٍ وَ رَشَّ بِهِ ثَوْبَهُ الْجَدِيدَ إِذَا لَبِسَهُ لَمْ يَزَلْ يَأْكُلُ فِي سَعَةٍ مَا بَقِيَ مِنْهُ سِلْكٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Muhammad, from Salih Bin Abu Hammad, from someone else, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one who recites <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:97#h1\"><a href=\"/books/quran:97#h1\">[97:1]</a></a> We have indeed revealed this </span>thirty two times in a new utensil, and sprinkle his new clothes with it when he wears it, he would be eating in ease (plentifully) for as long as a thread from it remains’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali ibn Muhammad has narrated from Salih ibn abu Hammad from more than one person who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If one reads Chapter 97 of the Quran thirty-two times on a bowl of water and sprinkles it on a new dress just before wearing it, he will continue to eat affluently as long as a fiber thereof is left with him.’” "
        ]
      }
